Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Build slides/ from src/, share Partie 1 of
 claude-on-scotch as its own deck
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

slides/ is now BUILT output; the sources move to src/:
  src/presentations/<name>.html  one full page per deck -> slides/<name>.html
  src/slides/*.html              one <section> or several, shared between decks

Either may embed any file under src/ with `<!-- @include slides/x.html -->`
alone on its line. build.js (bun, no dependencies) splices the file in
verbatim between `@begin` / `@end` marker comments, so a built deck says
where every slide came from; includes nest, a cycle is an error naming the
path, the same file may be included twice. `--check` builds in memory and
fails if slides/ is stale, missing a deck, or has a deck with no source.
tests/build.test.js covers the directive, nesting, missing files and cycles.

Partie 1 of claude-on-scotch (« Mon modèle mental des LLM », ~20 min) moves
verbatim to src/slides/mental-model-llm.html; the built claude-on-scotch is
the previous file plus the three marker comments and every other deck
rebuilds byte-identical. src/presentations/mental-model-of-llms.html is the
same part as a standalone talk (title, part, closing links).

The Makefile is the entry point (`make` lists the targets); every target is
a bun one-liner from package.json, so `bun run build` etc. work without
make. CI runs `make install`, `make browsers`, `make verify` (= check +
unit + e2e). index.html is generated from the writings repo and untouched;
the new deck needs an entry there.

