+
+      <!-- Python Downsides -->
+      <section>
+        <h2>Python Downsides</h2>
+        <ul>
+          <li><strong>Performance considerations</strong>
+            <ul>
+              <li>Interpreted with runtime type checking</li>
+              <li>Global Interpreter Lock (GIL) limits multithreading</li>
+              <li><strong>No tail call optimization</strong>
+                <ul>
+                  <li>Recursive functions have limited depth</li>
+                  <li>May need iterative solutions for deep recursion</li>
+                </ul>
+              </li>
+              <li>Rarely matters for most applications</li>
+              <li>Performance-critical code can use C/C++/Rust extensions</li>
+            </ul>
+          </li>
+        </ul>
